cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mvGPT in your work, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "mvGPT: a minimum viable GPT"
abstract: >-
  A small decoder-only transformer, written from scratch in PyTorch and readable
  from one end to the other, with 14.6 million parameters trained on
  TinyStories. It is the code of the YouTube series Minimum Viable GPT, which
  builds it one tagged step at a time and takes it through the training
  pipeline of a language model: pretraining, supervised fine-tuning, preference
  optimisation and reinforcement learning, then deployment.
authors:
  - given-names: Adrian Mircea
    family-names: Nenu
repository-code: "https://github.com/nenuadrian/mvGPT"
url: "https://mvgpt.nenuadrian.com"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - language model
  - transformer
  - GPT
  - PyTorch
  - reinforcement learning
  - education
